n completely we  don't need to see that  for any instance if you needed to see it  you could change it  you could hide it you could override it  depending how you want to showcase your  drawings  you have all these options at the click  of a button now obviously we go back to  hide it's a new construction  drawing so we don't want to see anything  but the  benefit and the biggest benefit in my  opinion of renovation layers is you  don't need  to worry about making errors and making  mistakes or if something changes in an  existing drawing  you don't have to go back and figure it  out change it and then go back to the  new construction  it was a very long time in my career  that we didn't use renovation filters  and having moved to renovation filters  it is an  absolute game changer now with a quick  little interlude i wanted to shout out  cuts clothing today they are an  incredible brand that i've been working  with for over a year now  and they just genuinely make the best  most comfortable t-shirts in the game  i wouldn't recommend them on this  channel if i thought they were garbage  you can go back through my channel for  years and years and years and almost  every single black shirt that i've ever  worn has been by cuts  so take a look at them there is a link  down below if you want to check them out  it would be greatly appreciated now  finally in this renovation settings  palette you're going to see  this little dialog box down the bottom  which has a series of different options  and depending on which renovation filter  you're on  different things are going to be enabled  and disabled  now we can go through these and change  them again to see  and suit how we like our documentation  so you can see on existing they've  hidden  all the opening dimension markers if i  untick it  you'll see all the dimension markers pop  up so they're more so labels for your  doors and your windows  if i tick it again they hide the solid  cut feel is a very  promising one and a 